  "steps": [
    "Valid saved animation opens in its independent module. Actual Rust sampling at 0.5s produces offset [60,-30]; play advances, pause holds, stop returns to zero without changing source or files.",
    "Edited keyframes require a fresh check before sampling or Apply. Review and exact Rust offset [80,-30] agree; Chinese/English/Japanese at 390px retain input node, focus, selection, checked draft and reachable footer actions. Cancel changes no author files.",
    "Invalid numeric input remains editable and clears old preview/approval. Adding a key chooses a valid time inside the current duration. Removing keys and adding/removing tracks preserve the ordinary draft, and detached old row buttons cannot mutate replacement rows.",
    "Apply updates only the ordinary source draft, reopening reads that unsaved draft, and Cancel retains it. Ordinary Save writes only the reviewed animation with BOM/CRLF preserved; the scene, actor, templates and registration files remain unchanged."
  ],
